Revert "pps: generate forward-looking counters"

This reverts upstream commit 2e6507f0e8bb569752b6aa8365dcffd96e3486c3,
which is in Mesa 26.2.5. It calls GpuCounterSpec::set_value_direction(),
which the board's Perfetto (chromeos-base/perfetto 53.0) does not have, so
pps-producer fails to compile:

  error: no member named 'set_value_direction' in
  'perfetto::protos::pbzero::GpuCounterDescriptor_GpuCounterSpec'

The commit's timestamp change depends on that field, so it is reverted
whole: pps keeps the end-of-interval counters 26.1.8 shipped. Drop this
when the board's Perfetto has value_direction.

